{number: 172}
{title: Near to the Heart of God}
{key: C}

{start_of_verse: 1}
There is a [C] place of quiet [F] rest,
[C] Near to the heart of [G7] God;
A place where [C] sin cannot mo-[F] lest,
[C] Near to the [G7] heart of [C] God.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus}
O [F] Jesus, blest Re-[C] deemer,
Sent [G7] from the heart of [C] God,
Hold [C] us who wait be-[F] fore Thee
[C] Near to the [G7] heart of [C] God.
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: 2}
There is a [C] place of comfort [F] sweet,
[C] Near to the heart of [G7] God;
A place where [C] we our Savior [F] meet,
[C] Near to the [G7] heart of [C] God.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: 3}
There is a [C] place of full re-[F] lease,
[C] Near to the heart of [G7] God;
A place where [C] all is joy and [F] peace,
[C] Near to the [G7] heart of [C] God.
{end_of_verse}
